[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
To start the relay, set paseo_relay_enable="YES" and run "service
paseo_relay start".  It listens on 127.0.0.1:4000 (paseo_relay_host,
paseo_relay_port) over plain HTTP.  Clients need TLS with a publicly
trusted certificate, so put a reverse proxy in front of it that forwards
/ws with WebSocket upgrades, and do not expose /metrics.

The relay has no authentication: anyone who can reach it can use it, and
anyone who knows a daemon's server ID can disconnect it.

To use it from a Paseo daemon (misc/paseo), set in its config.json:

    "daemon": { "relay": {
        "enabled": true,
        "endpoint": "127.0.0.1:4000", "useTls": false,
        "publicEndpoint": "relay.example.org:443", "publicUseTls": true
    } }

useTls defaults to false for endpoints other than relay.paseo.sh.  Pair
clients again after changing the relay.
EOM
}
]
